# TAZUNA: only what is listed below goes into the repository (an allow-list).
#
# Everything else in this folder stays on the robot's computer: run records and photos (runs/), old versions
# (backups/, with the un-wiped originals of the test photos), video material (video/), what is on the gripper
# right now (tool_active.json), which Python runs the harness here (config/python), review and research notes.
#
# - A new top-level file needs a line here, otherwise git does not see it.
# - Inside the published folders only the listed kinds of file are taken.
# - Photos are never taken by a pattern. A photo goes in only after someone has looked at it at full size and
#   wiped what should not be public: `git add -f <photo>`, then `python tools/publish/privacy_wipe.py accept`.
#   `python tools/publish/privacy_wipe.py check` refuses a tracked photo that is not on the reviewed list or
#   has changed (run it before every commit; a local pre-commit hook can do that).
# - NEVER run `git clean -x` or `git clean -X` here: for git all the private folders above are "ignored files",
#   and it would delete them.
# - `fd` rewrites some tracked files in normal use (config/config.json and the calibration files): read
#   `git diff` before a commit.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE
!/PROGRESS.md
!/README.md
!/fd
!/config/
!/docs/
!/examples/
!/tests/
!/tools/

# config/: the four files that hold the measurements of one rig
/config/**
!/config/config.json
!/config/camera_model.json
!/config/calib_points.json
!/config/probes.json

# docs/ and examples/: text (no photos). The two icons are the only pictures, named one by one; they are on the
# reviewed list too.
/docs/**
!/docs/**/
!/docs/**/*.md
!/docs/images/tazuna-icon.png
!/docs/images/tazuna-horse.png
/examples/**
!/examples/**/
!/examples/**/*.md

# tests/: the suites (*.py and README.md at the top), their data, the reference URDF and meshes. Private notes and
# test outputs lie in these folders on the robot's computer, so each folder takes only the kinds of file that are
# published from it.
/tests/*
!/tests/*.py
!/tests/README.md
!/tests/testdata/
!/tests/refs/
# tests/testdata/: recorded data (json, npy); photos only by `git add -f` (see the top of this file)
/tests/testdata/**
!/tests/testdata/**/
!/tests/testdata/**/*.json
!/tests/testdata/**/*.npy
# an unused copy of tools/prototypes/pen_draw/pen_state.json
/tests/testdata/pen_20261111/pen_state.json
# tests/refs/: only the URDF folder (urdf, xml, stl, the upstream README) and the gripper reference (py); not the
# review and research notes, and not the answers of the GitHub API about the upstream repository
/tests/refs/*
!/tests/refs/urdf/
!/tests/refs/gripper/
/tests/refs/urdf/**
!/tests/refs/urdf/**/
!/tests/refs/urdf/**/*.urdf
!/tests/refs/urdf/**/*.xml
!/tests/refs/urdf/**/*.stl
!/tests/refs/urdf/README.md
/tests/refs/gripper/**
!/tests/refs/gripper/**/
!/tests/refs/gripper/**/*.py

# tools/: the sources, one folder per feature
/tools/**
!/tools/**/
!/tools/**/*.py
!/tools/**/*.json
!/tools/**/*.md

__pycache__/
.*/
.#*
